# POS-payments — Requirements Impact Refinement (decision needed)

## Requirement revision

| Requirement ID | Revision | Decision | Supersedes |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `REQ-001` | Retry every failed charge automatically, while preserving the existing idempotency contract, keeping the pre-webhook payment state accurate, and preventing a timeout after capture from becoming a duplicate capture. The exact retry and reconciliation policy remains the pending decision. | `NEEDS_DECISION` | — |

## Current behavior and preserved invariants

| Invariant ID | Current behavior that must be preserved | Evidence level | Evidence |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `INV-001` | Charge requests accept an `idempotency_key`, which is the existing correlation mechanism for repeated requests. | `verified` | Supplied repository evidence: “charge requests accept an idempotency_key.” |
| `INV-002` | Payment status is rendered before webhook settlement, so an initial response can precede the provider’s final settlement event. | `verified` | Supplied repository evidence: “payment status is rendered before webhook settlement.” |
| `INV-003` | The provider may time out after capture, making a transport timeout insufficient to prove that no charge occurred. | `verified` | Supplied repository evidence: “the provider may time out after capture.” |

